+HSM / KMS Onboarding & Audit Runbook
+
+Objective
+- Provide a repeatable, auditable process to onboard KMS/HSM keys used for cosign, ensure rotation, and collect artifacts for independent cryptographic audit.
+
+Preconditions
+- A cloud KMS (AWS KMS / GCP KMS) or on-prem HSM available.
+- Vault installed and accessible; Vault operator credentials present.
+- Rekor (transparency log) and cosign installed in operator environment.
+
+Steps
+1. Provision KMS/HSM key
+   - Create a purpose-scoped key (e.g., "aegis/cosign-signing") with usage limited to sign/verify.
+   - Enable key rotation where supported; set rotation schedule (e.g., 90 days).
+   - Record key metadata: key ARN/ID, creation_time, rotation_policy.
+
+2. Create minimal IAM role or OIDC trust for CI runners
+   - Create a dedicated short-lived role for GitHub Actions to assume via OIDC with least privilege (kms:Sign, kms:GetPublicKey).
+   - Constrain trust policy by repo, branch, and optional conditions.
+
+3. Store KMS metadata in Vault
+   - Write KV secret at secret/aegis/cosign_kms with fields: uri, created_at, role_arn, notes.
+
+4. Smoke-sign and Rekor snapshot
+   - Use cosign with KMS URI to sign a small artifact.
+   - Verify signature with cosign verify and extract Rekor entry (rekor-cli).
+   - Save signature, Rekor UUID, and cosign verification output to an audit directory.
+
+5. Rotate keys (periodic)
+   - Rotate per rotation policy or when compromise suspected.
+   - For rotation: create new key, update Vault secret with new URI, run smoke-sign verification and Rekor snapshot, and archive previous key metadata.
+
+6. Audit collection
+   - Collect cosign version, Rekor server entries, Vault secret metadata and IAM role policy into a single archive for third-party auditors.
+   - Provide procedures to reproduce smoke-sign steps and to verify Rekor entries independently.
+
+Artifacts to provide to auditor
+- Vault secret snapshot (read-only view), cosign signature output, Rekor entry JSON, IAM trust policy, key metadata, and evidence manifests recorded by ops/sdk/evidence_sdk.
+
+Security notes
+- Private key material should never be exported from KMS/HSM.
+- Access to Vault paths and IAM roles must be tightly controlled and audited.
+
