+# Self-hosted Hardware CI Runner Security Guidance
+
+Best practices:
+- Place runners in isolated lab VPC or private network with no internet egress except to required registries.
+- Use ephemeral tokens for registration and rotate runner registration tokens.
+- Limit runner user accounts and use host-level hardening (SSH keys, disk encryption).
+- Restrict who can trigger workflows that run on hardware runners (branch protection, CODEOWNERS).
+- Ensure logs and artifacts are archived and recorded with evidence manifests.
+- Use resource quotas and cgroups to avoid noisy-neighbor effects on attached hardware.
